    Bug 2049194 - Fix "Run Now" button permanently disabled in filter dialog. r=mkmelin


    In bug 1985780 nsIMsgStatusFeedback was replaced with a postMessage-based
    FeedbackService that broadcasts start/stop-meteors globally to all windows.
    The filter dialog's stop-meteors handler accidentally commented out the
    line that re-enables gRunFiltersButton, so the button stayed permanently
    disabled after any meteors cycle — even from unrelated background operations
    like a mail poll in another window.

    Fix this by moving the button and gRunningFilters state management out of
    the global meteors handlers and into runSelectedFilters(), where it's clear
    that a filter run is actually starting. The message event listener now
    returns early unless gRunningFilters is true, preventing background
    operations from affecting the dialog's button state, progress bar, or
    status text.

    Also fix progressMeterVisible not being reset to false in stop-meteors,
    which prevented the progress bar from appearing on subsequent filter runs.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307966

